+# scripts/audit — executed evidence
+
+These are not guards. They do not run in `verify-all.mjs`, they do not gate a
+commit, and they never fail a build. They exist so that a claim in
+`docs/AUDIT_01_VISUALIZER.md` can be re-executed by anyone, on any checkout,
+against the real implementation rather than against a comment.
+
+Each script builds a synthetic room with **known ground truth**, runs it through
+the production function, and prints what actually happened.
+
+```bash
+node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings \
+  --import ./scripts/audit/register.mjs \
+  scripts/audit/occlusion.audit.ts      # AV-01: what survives on the floor
+
+node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings \
+  --import ./scripts/audit/register.mjs \
+  scripts/audit/boundary.audit.ts       # AV-02: is "measured" true
+```
+
+`ts-hook.mjs` resolves the repo's `@/` and `@ecowoods/shared/*` aliases so the
+scripts import the same modules the app does. Node ≥ 22.6 strips the types.
+
+When VIS-02 and VIS-03 land, these become vitest fixtures with an error budget.
+Until then they are the audit's working.
